---
import RootLayout from '../layouts/RootLayout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<RootLayout
  title="Terms of Service & Code of Play — Kirinyaga University Esports"
  description="Terms of service, tournament participation guidelines, prize distribution rules, and code of play for Kirinyaga University Esports and Tribe Campus."
>
  <Navbar />

  <main class="flex-1">
    <!-- Top Header Stage -->
    <section class="relative pt-12 pb-10 sm:pt-16 sm:pb-14 bg-black border-b border-[#202835]/80 overflow-hidden">
      <div
        class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 opacity-20"
        style="background: radial-gradient(circle at 50% 0%, rgba(251, 175, 23, 0.35), transparent 60%), radial-gradient(circle at 85% 60%, rgba(0, 161, 225, 0.2), transparent 50%);"
      >
      </div>

      <div class="padding-global relative z-10">
        <div class="container-large max-w-4xl mx-auto">
          <a
            href="/"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs sm:text-sm font-medium text-white/70 hover:text-[#fbaf17] transition-colors mb-6 group"
          >
            <svg class="w-4 h-4 transition-transform group-hover:-translate-x-1" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M11 17l-5-5m0 0l5-5m-5 5h12" />
            </svg>
            <span>Back to Home</span>
          </a>

          <h1 class="heading-hero text-white mb-4">
            Terms of Service &amp; <span class="text-yellow-highlight">Code of Play</span>
          </h1>

          <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-white/80 leading-relaxed">
            Last Updated: October 2026. By registering for the Kirinyaga University Esports roster, participating in campus tournaments, or joining our official WhatsApp clan channels, you agree to these terms.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Content Stage -->
    <section class="py-12 sm:py-16 lg:py-20 bg-[#121110]">
      <div class="padding-global">
        <div class="container-large max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-10 text-white/85 text-[15px] sm:text-[16px] leading-[1.75]">
          
          <!-- Summary Box -->
          <div class="p-5 sm:p-6 rounded-2xl bg-[#191f2a] border border-[#202835] space-y-2">
            <span class="font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#fbaf17] block">
              Core Principles (Quick Read)
            </span>
            <p class="text-sm text-white/90">
              1. Registration is 100% free for KyU students. <br />
              2. Play fair: zero cheats, hacks, or ringers allowed. <br />
              3. Keep community channels respectful: zero tolerance for harassment, bullying, or hate speech. <br />
              4. Prizes are credited in Carry1st Discount Points (CDP) to verified Carry1st Shop profiles.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Section 1 -->
          <div class="space-y-3">
            <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2.5">
              <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-[#fbaf17]"></span>
              1. Eligibility &amp; Student Verification
            </h2>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1.5 text-white/80">
              <li><strong class="text-white">Active Student Status:</strong> Participation in official KyU varsity divisions, seeded tournaments, and campus leagues is restricted to currently enrolled Kirinyaga University students.</li>
              <li><strong class="text-white">Accurate Credentials:</strong> You must supply your authentic student registration number and institutional email. Registering with fraudulent or third-party admission numbers results in instant disqualification.</li>
              <li><strong class="text-white">Free Access:</strong> Membership in the club and regular tournament participation carries zero entry fees or subscription charges.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <!-- Section 2 -->
          <div class="space-y-3">
            <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2.5">
              <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-[#00a1e1]"></span>
              2. Carry1st Rewards &amp; CDP Distribution
            </h2>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1.5 text-white/80">
              <li><strong class="text-white">CDP Currency:</strong> Tournament prize pools, participation drops, and challenge bonuses are distributed as Carry1st Discount Points (CDP).</li>
              <li><strong class="text-white">Valid Shop Profile:</strong> Players must maintain a registered Carry1st Shop account with the email specified during registration. Points cannot be credited to unverified or invalid accounts.</li>
              <li><strong class="text-white">Redemptions:</strong> CDP can be redeemed via the Carry1st Shop for supported digital products, including mobile airtime, data bundles, game currencies (COD Points, eFootball coins, Free Fire diamonds), and vouchers. Points are governed by Carry1st platform terms and conditions.</li>
              <li><strong class="text-white">No Direct Cash Guarantee:</strong> Campus budget distributions are allocated in CDP. Any cash or physical conversions are subject to regional Carry1st coordinator approval according to official Tribe Campus guidelines.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <!-- Section 3 -->
          <div class="space-y-3">
            <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2.5">
              <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-[#22c55e]"></span>
              3. Competitive Integrity &amp; Fair Play
            </h2>
            <p>
              To maintain fair competition for all students, the following actions will trigger immediate match forfeiture, prize revocation, and possible seasonal bans:
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1.5 text-white/80">
              <li><strong class="text-white">Third-Party Exploits:</strong> Use of hacks, aimbots, wallhacks, scripts, memory modifiers, or unauthorized emulators in mobile-restricted divisions.</li>
              <li><strong class="text-white">Ringers &amp; Smurfs:</strong> Playing under another student's account or bringing in non-KyU players to substitute in official matches.</li>
              <li><strong class="text-white">Match Fixing &amp; Collusion:</strong> Intentionally manipulating match outcomes, bracket seeding, or prize splits.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <!-- Section 4 -->
          <div class="space-y-3">
            <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2.5">
              <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-[#fbaf17]"></span>
              4. Community Guidelines &amp; Channel Decorum
            </h2>
            <p>
              In alignment with the Tribe Campus Leaders Handbook, all club interactions—whether in WhatsApp groups, Discord rooms, or physical hangouts—must respect the following standards:
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1.5 text-white/80">
              <li><strong class="text-white">Everyone is a Gamer:</strong> We welcome casual and hardcore gamers alike. Gatekeeping, elitism, and belittling beginner players is strictly forbidden.</li>
              <li><strong class="text-white">Zero Tolerance:</strong> Threats of violence (direct or implied), cyberbullying, hate speech, sexual harassment, explicit/pornographic content, and gore will result in immediate removal and escalation to university administration if warranted.</li>
              <li><strong class="text-white">No Spam or Commercial Promotion:</strong> Campus gaming channels are for matchmaking, tournament updates, and gaming discussions. No commercial ads, political propaganda, or unrelated solicitations.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <!-- Section 5 -->
          <div class="space-y-3">
            <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2.5">
              <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-[#00a1e1]"></span>
              5. Academic Balance &amp; University Affiliation
            </h2>
            <p>
              Esports activities are scheduled outside official lecture hours, lab sessions, and examination periods. The club emphasizes responsible academic balance. While the club operates with student leadership and university sporting recognition, academic commitments remain the student's primary priority.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Section 6 -->
          <div class="space-y-3">
            <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2.5">
              <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-[#22c55e]"></span>
              6. Disciplinary Enforcement
            </h2>
            <p>
              Campus leaders and community coordinators reserve the authority to issue warnings, forfeit matches, deduct tournament points, or expel disruptive individuals from club channels. Appeals can be directed to the student secretariat via official email channels.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- CTA Banner -->
          <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-[#161b25] border border-[#202835] flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between gap-4">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white mb-1">Ready to play?</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-white/70">Join hundreds of fellow KyU students in the official gaming roster.</p>
            </div>
            <a href="/register" class="primary-button-gold shrink-0 justify-center">
              <span>Join Free</span>
            </a>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</RootLayout>
